# Request: step k of one person (hakoniwa-robot-runtime#17, hakoniwa-scenario-pro memo 018).
# The runtime steps only when every robot's step-k request has arrived.
# step: step number k
# cmd_vel: walking velocity in the person's own frame, as ROS cmd_vel (base_link):
#          linear.x forward, linear.y left, angular.z turn rate (rad/s)
# animation: auto (or empty), stand, talk, sit_talk, ... as the people PDU
# ride: "<vehicle>/<seat>" to ride, empty to stay on foot
uint64 step
geometry_msgs/Twist cmd_vel
string animation
string ride
---
# Response: the person after step k was applied and the world stepped once
# step: the request's k; result_code: 0 ok
# sim_time_usec: Hakoniwa time after the step
# pose / twist: world frame, ROS axes (x north, y west, z up)
# joints: shoulder, hip, knee, ... angles (the same names as the people JointState)
uint64 step
uint32 result_code
uint64 sim_time_usec
geometry_msgs/Transform pose
geometry_msgs/Twist twist
sensor_msgs/JointState joints
